                        "form": "ностальги́ях"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f0151e34-f8b6-37ca-8588-70878f6a21b6",
                        "entry_id": "6d4a1ccd-0f20-3bfd-abd8-b898352e6a79",
                        "glosses": [
                            "книжн. болезненная тоска по родине, по родному краю, по связи с домом"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "7c545738-618c-4fa8-a32b-89e55f3341e7",
                                "sense_id": "f0151e34-f8b6-37ca-8588-70878f6a21b6",
                                "text": "У них просыпается ностальгия, они начинают обещать, что прямо следующим летом приедут в Москву или Питер, хотя многие из них не были на родине лет шесть и совсем не скучали."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "38bb3f48-7606-3580-85ea-31c66c3cf3ea",
                        "entry_id": "6d4a1ccd-0f20-3bfd-abd8-b898352e6a79",
                        "glosses": [
                            "разг. болезненная тоска по прошлому"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "be7c8b6b-29d5-47cc-9b45-528e7c02c630",
                                "sense_id": "38bb3f48-7606-3580-85ea-31c66c3cf3ea",
                                "text": "В этом сочетании слов слышалось нечто школьно-будничное и общедоступное, в то время как в коротком «физик» заключалась ностальгия по тем временам, когда профессия эта была ещё в почёте."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f6283824-156b-4305-a4aa-27e0e65daeb5",
                        "source_entry_id": "6d4a1ccd-0f20-3bfd-abd8-b898352e6a79",
                        "target_lang_word": "nostalgia",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "nostalgia",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9c9ee7c1-c4a9-3658-941e-98805034c3ba",
                                        "entry_id": "4436fcd4-9b7c-341d-b4b2-74b28660add7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A longing for home or familiar surroundings; homesickness."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncommon",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e3df9418-fedd-4de0-8614-0079c0d7efa6",
                                                "sense_id": "9c9ee7c1-c4a9-3658-941e-98805034c3ba",
                                                "text": "Seeing food at camp similar to his mother's cooking sent a wave of nostalgia through him."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "237a08d7-9f5b-4fd9-b05c-e0a30f60e741",
                                                "sense_id": "9c9ee7c1-c4a9-3658-941e-98805034c3ba",
                                                "text": "I have an idea that some men are born out of their due place. Accident has cast them amid certain surroundings, but they have always a nostalgia for a home they know not."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "68fd1365-7d14-37fe-bf9f-e87028d020ca",
                                        "entry_id": "4436fcd4-9b7c-341d-b4b2-74b28660add7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A bittersweet yearning for the things of the past."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3e20deef-71fc-46c8-96c4-48bf9e024e74",
                                                "sense_id": "68fd1365-7d14-37fe-bf9f-e87028d020ca",
                                                "text": "an alumnus' feelings of nostalgia for his/her years in high school"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d1c29e5e-7fbb-426a-91ca-d038383af9e5",
                                                "sense_id": "68fd1365-7d14-37fe-bf9f-e87028d020ca",
                                                "text": "I can't have been the only person, last week, to feel a rush of nostalgia upon learning that Thames Water had removed a bus-sized, 15-tonne lump of food fat (\"mixed with wet wipes\") from the sewers under London. The fatberg was an August news story redolent of the old-fashioned silly season."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2fa48bb3-7358-4a23-b90d-2fe56006549f",
                                                "sense_id": "68fd1365-7d14-37fe-bf9f-e87028d020ca",
                                                "text": "[…]Rousteing asked: “Is my generation’s nostalgia for our turn-of-the-century childhood culture somehow less cool than fashion’s more familiar fixation on the 70s and 80s?” The answer was a firm “no”: in 2020 all nostalgia is good nostalgia. “The nostalgia economy”, as named by Quartz, is the most powerful trend in fashion since florals or trousers and is a reaction to what’s happening in the world."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6ef81f41-71bf-4761-a2d8-327ec94886f9",
                                                "sense_id": "68fd1365-7d14-37fe-bf9f-e87028d020ca",
                                                "text": "Though there is nothing generationally unique in the desire to bask in the banalities of your past, these nostalgia communities have flourished on Facebook as its user base has grown ever older in the past decade."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9bc4a977-7506-405e-bdf6-9643998e15f5",
                                                "sense_id": "68fd1365-7d14-37fe-bf9f-e87028d020ca",
                                                "text": "Yet it continued to be treated as rather suspect. In the mid-20th century, a psychoanalyst called Nandor Fodor dismissed nostalgia, along with utopian politics and even the vogue for Tarzan films, as “the manifestation of a latent desire to return to the womb”."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "b01228c6-aea2-4638-9e10-88e02c07f4d2",
                        "source_entry_id": "6d4a1ccd-0f20-3bfd-abd8-b898352e6a79",
                        "target_lang_word": "homesickness",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "homesickness",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a3365007-de0e-3fc3-933d-dbc36bb9edd9",
                                        "entry_id": "949fa656-1445-3188-9fd2-8c253c46383b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The characteristic of being homesick; a strong, sad feeling of missing one's home (and often left-behind loved ones, such as family and friends) when physically away."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d5865de5-7f32-496c-93a8-a736a138e2e8",
                        "source_entry_id": "6d4a1ccd-0f20-3bfd-abd8-b898352e6a79",
                        "target_lang_word": "nostalgie",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "nostalgie",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "614d13bd-c7be-3163-8dae-311a50e68faa",
                                        "entry_id": "f1177e63-6d24-3aa4-8011-77034adc2d69",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Souffrance causée par le regret obsédant de la patrie ; mal du pays."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c65784e0-78f7-494c-9e6f-d383df9f6dd2",
                                                "sense_id": "614d13bd-c7be-3163-8dae-311a50e68faa",
                                                "text": "En dépit de son bon vouloir, de sa passion pour le travail, le désespoir d'être loin des siens l'emportait chez Pasteur. Le mal du pays l'envahissait. Jamais le mot de nostalgie ne fut d'une application plus juste."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ff293e69-9df2-4a75-836a-90ea7c508a83",
                                                "sense_id": "614d13bd-c7be-3163-8dae-311a50e68faa",
                                                "text": "— Vous allez pas nous déballer toutes vos cartes postales, non ? Le couplet sur Paris, voilà deux ans qu’on en croque. Ça revient comme du chou : Les petits bistros pas chers, les gambilles du samedi, la place du Tertre et le zouave du pont de l’Alma. Et dans cinq minutes, y en aura un qui va sortir un ticket de métro ou des photos de la Foire du Trône. Non, pour moi tout ça c’est râpé. Y’a plus de Paris. Y’a groß Paris. Un point, c’est marre !\n— Seriez vous insensible à la nostalgie, brigadier Dudu ?\n— Non ! Mais j’aime pas pas penser à reculons. Je laisse ça aux lopes et aux écrevisses."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7dc2043e-6601-40c3-9057-40b85bb2b096",
                                                "sense_id": "614d13bd-c7be-3163-8dae-311a50e68faa",
                                                "text": "Trump a misé sur la nostalgie pour l’emporter et si les défis du 21ᵉ siècle exigent qu’on s’adapte à de nouvelles réalités, on ne peut balayer du revers de la main les craintes d’une portion de la population blanche face à la mondialisation, l’immigration ou la croissance démographique."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2d7493ae-25cc-34cc-844f-3d75f4b41442",
                                        "entry_id": "f1177e63-6d24-3aa4-8011-77034adc2d69",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Regrets, non seulement d’un pays, mais d’un milieu auquel on a cessé d’appartenir, d’un genre de vie qu’on a cessé de mener, d'amis qu'on a perdus, d'un passé qui ne reviendra pas."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "analogy"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8d3a3d22-bfe4-412b-8fab-246400c7d81f",
                                                "sense_id": "2d7493ae-25cc-34cc-844f-3d75f4b41442",
                                                "text": "Amis alsaciens, c'est décidément bien vrai, vous êtes d'éternels inassouvis, les dilettantes obstinés d'un mécontentement fondamental ; vous avez toujours la nostalgie d'un je ne sais quoi qui n'existait pas hier et qui ne sera pas demain ; […]."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5d3db22e-f503-4864-8dba-604ec875a794",
                                                "sense_id": "2d7493ae-25cc-34cc-844f-3d75f4b41442",
                                                "text": "M. Hauriou a tout à l'heure formulé un rêve et manifesté une nostalgie : ceux d'un meilleur des univers politiques possibles, où les partis politiques vivraient dans un climat d’euphorie et se trouveraient parfaitement justifiés, parfaitement admis par l'opinion publique et parfaitement aimés."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c12a8006-298a-4b9c-bd84-ac81cf50217f",
                                                "sense_id": "2d7493ae-25cc-34cc-844f-3d75f4b41442",
                                                "text": "Petits Ritals, faites comme moi, barbouillez-vous de nostalgie, c’est un plaisir délicat que seuls peuvent s’offrir les déracinés, mais rien qu’un doigt, petits Ritals ! La nostalgie, c’est comme tout, t’en prends t’en laisses, tu prends le bon, tu laisses le reste…"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c7c59b83-f609-472d-bd80-b6ab74ae2d39",
